Package: tidyarena
Title: Benchmark Arena for 'dplyr' Backends
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Theo", "Blauberg", , "ma.oon.theo@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("H2O.ai, DuckDB Labs and the db-benchmark contributors", role = "cph",
           comment = "db-benchmark data generators and questions, see inst/COPYRIGHTS"),
    person("Ursa Computing", role = "cph",
           comment = "TPC-H-derived queries from arrowbench, see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
  )
Description: Runs one suite of 'dplyr' pipelines on many backends
    ('dplyr', 'dtplyr', 'duckplyr', 'dbplyr' with 'duckdb', 'arrow',
    'tidypolars', 'cuplyr') and records time, peak memory, coverage and
    correctness, together with a snapshot of the machine and its settings.
    Each task runs in its own R process under a memory budget, so a
    benchmark run cannot exhaust the machine. Results are written in a
    documented format meant for comparison across machines.
